hurries:
Under the dying stars.
A lonely newsboy hurries by,
Humming a recent ditty;

hurled:
Heigho, but the world is gloomy;
The light has failed and the lamp down hurled,
Leaves only darkness to me.

hurtle:
As sword that, after battle, flings to sheathe;
And, in that hurtle of united souls,
The mystic motions which in common moods

hurl'd:
To blacken Phoebus, and dissolve the sky;
His too, when all in his dark realms are hurl'd,
From its firm base to shake the solid world;
